  action: ANNOTATED
  changes: 'Edison LITERATURE (PaperQA3) identity research; report at research/ingredients/Bacto_Heart_Infusion_Broth-edison-literature.md
    (local artifact — research/ is gitignored, so the findings are quoted here rather
    than linked). Report verdict: **Recommended interpretation:** a **supplier-branded,
    dehydrated complete microbiological broth medium**, not a single chemical, salt/hydrate,
    buffer, or tissue extract alone. “Bacto” and “Difco” are trademarks associated
    with Difco products now supplied by BD; therefore, “Bacto Heart Infusion Broth”
    carries supplier/formulation scope rather than merely naming a generic chemical
    substance. The pre No ontology CURIE was proposed. Recorded as provenance only
    — no grounding applied from this run. Edison''s recommendations are deliberately
    conservative, and a plausible identifier promoted by a mechanism that never decided
    anything is what #203 and #263 exist to undo. Any CURIE above is a curator''s
    to accept or reject.'
